From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ps4-gladius <ps4-gladius@invalid>
Date: Tue, 7 Oct 2026 19:55:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] server: report the errno behind each NTSTATUS.

file_set_error() is where every failed system call in the server becomes an
NTSTATUS. By the time the caller sees the status the errno is gone, and a
status like 0xc0000022 (STATUS_ACCESS_DENIED) names a dozen possible sites --
create_user_data_mapping reaches it through several.

Log the errno and the caller's return address, which together identify the
failing call exactly.
---
diff --git a/server/file.c b/server/file.c
index 20680ef5b3..331741ba34 100644
--- a/server/file.c
+++ b/server/file.c
@@ -572,6 +572,24 @@ static void file_destroy( struct object *obj )
 /* set the last error depending on errno */
 void file_set_error(void)
 {
+#ifdef __PROSPERO__
+    /* ⚠ DIAGNOSTIC. This is where every failed syscall in the server becomes an
+     * NTSTATUS, and the errno it came from is the only thing that says which
+     * call failed. Without it a status such as 0xc0000022 (ACCESS_DENIED) names
+     * a dozen possible sites. */
+    {
+        extern int sceKernelDebugOutText( int channel, const char *text );
+        char line[128];
+        /* ⚠ Print this function's own address too. Module bases move between
+         * runs and a crash dump's library list is only there when the title
+         * actually crashes -- a clean exit leaves the return address
+         * unmappable. base = (this address) - (file_set_error's offset in the
+         * unstripped .shared.elf), which makes every other address resolvable. */
+        snprintf( line, sizeof(line), "wineserver: file_set_error errno=%d from %p (anchor %p)\n",
+                  errno, __builtin_return_address(0), (void *)(uintptr_t)&file_set_error );
+        sceKernelDebugOutText( 0, line );
+    }
+#endif
     switch (errno)
     {
     case ETXTBSY:
